/-!
# Finite generator-image rigidity for M11

Write a and b for the ATLAS generators. Once an automorphism fixes a,
its image y of b satisfies y^4 = (ay)^11 = (a y a y² a y⁻¹)^3 = 1.
Checking the 7920 Schreier coordinates leaves exactly the 48 conjugates
of b by C_M11(a). The witness function below records their conjugators;
the exhaustive identities are checked by Lean's kernel.

This gives the concrete automorphism calculation of GLS3, Table 5.3a.
The generator script discovers witnesses; it is not part of the proof.
-/

